==============================================================================
== verdict
==============================================================================
  The band responds to the surface out to about r_eq+0.16 = 2.00 A.
  EOM-CCSD is trusted to 2.4 A; 3A' becomes the lowest triplet from 2.55 A.
  -> 0.40 A of margin: a CCSD(T) + EOM raster to ~2.4 A with an absorber
     beyond is enough for sigma(lambda, T), as for HOCl. The crossing is product-
     branching scope, not band scope.

  First look at the deliverable, band aligned to the measured peak: sigma(298)/sigma(220)
  over 440-500 nm spans 0.972-0.990, i.e. -2.8% to -1.0%, from O-Br stretch hot bands alone.
  In the red wing: +4% at 520 nm, +20% at 550 nm, where sigma is a third of the peak and less.
  So in this model the temperature effect is NOT in the 440-500 nm window TASKS.md's
  impact threshold names -- it is below the 5% 'negligible' line there -- but in the red
  wing. Whether that wing matters is a J-value question: at high solar zenith angle the
  actinic flux shifts red. Caveats: a 1D band is too narrow, which exaggerates wing
  ratios, and the model sits 20 nm blue, so the alignment is itself an assumption the
  3D model and the SOC splitting have to remove.

